WEBVTT

00:02.530 --> 00:03.310
What?

00:03.310 --> 00:05.230
You saw it on TV too?

00:06.270 --> 00:07.560
I'm embarrassed.

00:07.560 --> 00:11.740
Those dolphins there, all of them were saved, right?

00:11.740 --> 00:13.030
That was amazing.

00:13.450 --> 00:14.510
Thank you.

00:15.010 --> 00:18.830
I do feel a bit proud about being a mage now.

00:18.830 --> 00:21.750
Sora, you sure are giving your best in Tokyo.

00:24.020 --> 00:25.500
Oh, by the way!

00:25.500 --> 00:28.840
I've made new friends and they're all mages.

00:28.840 --> 00:30.300
Good for you!

00:30.300 --> 00:32.840
By the way, have you gotten a boyfriend yet?

00:32.840 --> 00:34.930
Geez, Michiru you idiot!

00:34.930 --> 00:35.760
Oh?

00:35.760 --> 00:37.120
That's suspicious.

00:39.040 --> 00:40.520
How about you, Michiru?

00:42.070 --> 00:44.940
I will meet Toyama-kun next time.

00:44.940 --> 00:45.890
Really?

00:45.890 --> 00:47.230
That's great.

00:47.230 --> 00:51.650
It's all thanks to you, thanks for the snow.

00:55.080 --> 00:57.450
Good work yesterday.

00:57.450 --> 00:58.310
Yep.

01:01.940 --> 01:05.620
I said something arrogant yesterday by the sea.

01:05.620 --> 01:06.600
I'm sorry.

01:07.730 --> 01:08.880
Hey,

01:08.880 --> 01:11.800
I'd prefer you apologize before thanking me.

01:11.800 --> 01:12.610
Huh?

01:13.090 --> 01:16.050
Thanks to you, I can now use magic.

01:17.140 --> 01:19.720
That was the first time that I was able to use such power.

01:21.470 --> 01:25.770
It's not really a way to say thanks, but there is a place I want to take you to.

01:26.240 --> 01:27.980
A place you want to take me to?

01:28.530 --> 01:29.250
Yeah.

03:19.310 --> 03:19.920
The sea?

03:20.730 --> 03:23.820
Yes, you can say it's the sea. It's called Enoshima.

03:24.340 --> 03:26.470
Is that the place you want to take me?

03:27.400 --> 03:28.260
It's still a secret.

03:35.640 --> 03:38.820
Being here together almost looks like we're out on a date.

03:38.820 --> 03:40.100
You know...

03:40.430 --> 03:41.610
you don't need to add "looks like."

03:58.100 --> 03:59.840
I'm hungry.

03:59.840 --> 04:01.420
I'm starved, too.

04:02.230 --> 04:05.300
I know a place with good food, although it's a bit of a walk.

04:07.260 --> 04:09.810
I often go there after I'm done surfing.

04:12.980 --> 04:16.860
Gouta-kun, on your first day, when Saori-sensei got mad at you,

04:16.860 --> 04:18.470
didn't you go surfing after that?

04:19.300 --> 04:19.980
Yeah.

04:20.650 --> 04:25.610
I already decided when I was returning home by train that I was not going to surf for a while.

04:25.610 --> 04:26.790
Why?

04:27.390 --> 04:28.360
I'm not really sure.

04:29.330 --> 04:33.370
I probably thought it was a way of escaping from magic.

04:34.140 --> 04:35.250
That's admirable.

04:36.370 --> 04:37.760
It isn't.

04:39.080 --> 04:43.510
Somehow, for a little while, I thought it'd be better not to surf.

05:01.580 --> 05:02.820
This is delicious!

05:02.820 --> 05:03.520
Right?

05:05.100 --> 05:08.200
You know, the first time that we met,

05:08.200 --> 05:12.200
I got off at the wrong bus stop and had to walk a lot.

05:12.200 --> 05:14.830
The magic you performed back then was amazing.

05:14.830 --> 05:17.420
But you yelled at me.

05:18.060 --> 05:19.980
At that time, a lot of things had happened to me.

05:20.790 --> 05:22.340
My mother had just left our home...

05:22.340 --> 05:23.500
so I felt down.

05:23.970 --> 05:25.180
Your mother?

05:26.670 --> 05:28.440
This squid's soy sauce is delicious.

05:29.410 --> 05:30.100
Yes.

05:32.720 --> 05:33.960
Wow!

05:34.780 --> 05:36.240
Amazing!

05:37.230 --> 05:38.760
The sea is glistening!

05:39.170 --> 05:39.870
Yeah.

05:56.320 --> 05:57.090
Hello?

05:58.700 --> 06:00.880
Um, Midorikawa-kun?

06:00.880 --> 06:02.590
It's Yamabuki.

06:02.590 --> 06:03.540
What's the matter?

06:04.560 --> 06:06.590
What are you doing now?

06:06.590 --> 06:07.550
Well...

06:09.670 --> 06:10.990
I am looking at the sea now.

06:12.630 --> 06:13.380
It's Yamabuki.

06:14.230 --> 06:15.520
Are you with someone?

06:15.520 --> 06:17.020
Yeah, with Suzuki.

06:19.140 --> 06:20.910
It's great that the weather is so nice.

06:21.480 --> 06:22.400
Yeah it is.

06:22.400 --> 06:24.690
Well, since it's the last day of vacation,

06:24.690 --> 06:27.600
I was thinking of going somewhere with everyone.

06:27.980 --> 06:28.820
I see.

06:28.820 --> 06:29.940
I hadn't thought of that.

06:30.360 --> 06:32.390
You sure think of everyone, Yamabuki.

06:33.100 --> 06:34.250
I guess.

06:34.830 --> 06:36.240
I'm sorry for today.

06:36.240 --> 06:37.050
It's okay.

06:37.860 --> 06:39.620
Please say "Hi" to Sora-chan for me.

06:39.620 --> 06:41.100
Okay, later then.

06:52.480 --> 06:53.250
Yes?

06:53.660 --> 06:54.620
Where are you now?

06:55.260 --> 06:56.490
In my room.

06:57.580 --> 06:59.390
You sound depressed.

06:59.390 --> 07:00.600
Did anything happen?

07:00.600 --> 07:01.310
Yeah.

07:01.890 --> 07:04.680
What are you doing inside on such a nice day?

07:05.190 --> 07:06.810
Feeling miserable.

07:07.350 --> 07:09.360
Want to come eat some huge soft ice cream?

07:10.420 --> 07:13.330
There's a store in Nagano which serves large portions of soft ice cream.

07:13.810 --> 07:14.540
I'll go!

07:15.920 --> 07:17.640
Hey, wait for me.

07:19.620 --> 07:20.870
Come on, come on!

07:26.490 --> 07:27.490
It's beautiful!

07:29.460 --> 07:32.900
This sea... I want my mother to see it too.

07:33.590 --> 07:35.340
You could bring her here next time.

07:36.200 --> 07:37.290
You're right.

07:46.950 --> 07:48.070
Is he lost?

07:56.890 --> 07:59.040
Now, can you see your father?

07:59.710 --> 08:01.100
Can you see your mother?

08:01.740 --> 08:03.000
Maybe I can.

08:03.000 --> 08:04.460
Don't you see them?

08:04.460 --> 08:06.460
I wonder where my mother is.

08:07.250 --> 08:10.210
Let's ask at that beach hut to make a lost child announcement.

08:10.210 --> 08:12.550
Hey, what's your name?

08:12.550 --> 08:15.330
I won't tell my name to people I don't know.

08:16.220 --> 08:18.010
Then is it alright for you to ride on my back?

08:18.010 --> 08:19.540
Riding on your back is okay!

08:21.970 --> 08:23.140
How troublesome.

08:23.140 --> 08:24.550
Sota!

08:25.210 --> 08:25.900
Mama!

08:26.340 --> 08:27.480
Sota!

08:27.480 --> 08:30.400
I'm sorry, he's my child!

08:30.400 --> 08:31.610
Geez!

08:31.610 --> 08:34.450
Didn't I tell you not to run off on your own?

08:34.450 --> 08:35.930
But...

08:36.490 --> 08:38.020
He sure is an energetic child.

08:39.300 --> 08:41.330
I'm really sorry to have troubled you.

08:41.330 --> 08:43.000
My apologies.

08:43.000 --> 08:44.540
That's great, isn't it?

08:44.540 --> 08:45.330
Yep.

08:45.900 --> 08:47.650
Mama, I am thirsty.

08:50.670 --> 08:52.650
This child is... really...

08:53.850 --> 08:55.010
We're sorry.

08:55.010 --> 08:55.970
Bye!

08:55.970 --> 08:57.040
Bye!

08:59.330 --> 09:00.260
Bye-bye!

09:00.260 --> 09:02.060
Hey, I was really worried.

09:02.060 --> 09:03.430
Mom, hurry up.

09:03.430 --> 09:04.640
So his name is Sota.

09:04.640 --> 09:05.890
The same "So" from Sora.

09:05.890 --> 09:07.120
And the same "ta" from Gota.

09:10.460 --> 09:12.640
Sota-kun was so cute.

09:13.060 --> 09:14.210
His mother too.

09:17.370 --> 09:18.900
I was just kidding.

09:19.450 --> 09:21.380
Sora, wait up!

09:33.250 --> 09:34.260
Welcome.

09:35.370 --> 09:37.220
Oh, fresh little sardines!

09:37.220 --> 09:37.970
Looks foolishly delicious.

09:37.220 --> 09:41.220
The expression "bakauma" (馬鹿馬) consists of baka (fool) and umai (delicious). Used in the Hakata dialect of southern Kyushu.

09:38.960 --> 09:41.220
It looks like an eating festival.

09:49.500 --> 09:51.060
What is "Esukaa"?

09:52.560 --> 09:56.490
You can either go up the stairs, or take the Esca.

09:56.910 --> 09:58.860
Looks kind of futuristic.

09:58.860 --> 10:00.050
That's anti-gravity.

10:03.230 --> 10:05.870
Is this anti-gravity?

10:05.870 --> 10:07.850
It's my first time riding it too.

10:11.630 --> 10:13.210
Oh, fortune telling!

10:15.540 --> 10:16.980
How was yours, Gouta?

10:17.720 --> 10:20.760
Mine is just normal luck.

10:21.420 --> 10:22.220
How about yours?

10:22.220 --> 10:23.550
Let's see...

10:24.080 --> 10:24.970
Oh!

10:24.970 --> 10:25.830
What's the matter?

10:26.410 --> 10:27.730
It's nothing.

10:28.200 --> 10:29.350
I want to see it.

10:29.350 --> 10:30.310
You can't.

10:30.310 --> 10:30.940
What?

10:30.940 --> 10:31.900
Why is that?

10:31.900 --> 10:32.980
A no is a no!

10:32.980 --> 10:34.500
Show it to me, hey!

10:40.080 --> 10:43.020
The place you wanted to show me, was it here?

10:44.750 --> 10:45.490
It's a secret.

10:46.920 --> 10:48.230
So, shall we get going?

10:48.690 --> 10:49.910
We still have to walk a little bit.

10:51.910 --> 10:53.630
There are many hilly paths.

10:54.100 --> 10:54.900
Are you all right?

10:55.520 --> 10:57.000
Is it still far?

10:57.000 --> 10:58.320
We're almost there.

11:12.300 --> 11:14.770
Welcome, please sit wherever you'd like.

11:14.770 --> 11:15.640
Okay.

11:21.870 --> 11:22.780
This place?

11:23.460 --> 11:24.180
Yes.

11:28.520 --> 11:29.520
It's beautiful.

11:40.290 --> 11:43.130
The first time that I came here, I was surprised too.

11:43.130 --> 11:45.340
This place is really amazing.

11:46.350 --> 11:47.220
Here you go.

11:47.220 --> 11:48.640
What is this?

11:48.640 --> 11:50.390
Oh, it's big!

11:50.390 --> 11:52.060
How nice, you came here with your dad.

11:52.060 --> 11:54.310
There's no way that I can drink it like this!

11:54.310 --> 11:57.080
If you use the straw, then you can drink it, right?

11:57.960 --> 11:59.050
Oh, I see.

11:59.650 --> 12:00.480
Ah, sorry.

12:00.480 --> 12:01.650
Could I get some pickles?

12:01.650 --> 12:02.530
Yes.

12:05.030 --> 12:06.910
Children are fun, aren't they?

12:06.910 --> 12:07.620
Yeah.

12:07.620 --> 12:08.950
When is the next time you have a day off?

12:09.410 --> 12:10.450
Who knows.

12:10.450 --> 12:11.620
Is it tomorrow?

12:11.620 --> 12:12.580
I have work.

12:12.580 --> 12:13.710
And the day after?

12:13.710 --> 12:14.830
Work.

12:14.830 --> 12:16.420
Then the day after that?

12:16.420 --> 12:17.490
Work.

12:18.530 --> 12:19.880
And the day after that?

12:19.880 --> 12:20.840
A day off, perhaps?

12:20.840 --> 12:22.300
Can we play then?

12:22.300 --> 12:23.090
Yes.

12:23.090 --> 12:23.860
Oh?

12:25.200 --> 12:26.350
It'll get cold.

12:27.480 --> 12:29.810
What's in the Enoshima-don?

12:27.480 --> 12:30.690
Enoshima-don is a local food: Grilled strips of sazae in an egg mixture on rice. Sazae = mollusk known as Turban shell.

12:29.810 --> 12:30.690
Sazae.

12:32.450 --> 12:33.770
Give me your hand.

12:38.220 --> 12:39.200
A present.

12:43.800 --> 12:44.510
This is...

12:45.020 --> 12:46.750
I picked this up at the sea yesterday.

12:47.820 --> 12:48.990
A gem of the sea.

12:50.000 --> 12:50.950
It's beautiful.

12:50.950 --> 12:53.240
Yes, it's a souvenir.

12:55.100 --> 12:55.780
Thank you.

13:16.420 --> 13:17.770
Over here. Here.

13:17.770 --> 13:19.390
Hurry up!

13:20.280 --> 13:22.020
Say, say, will you give me a piggy-back ride?

13:22.020 --> 13:22.780
What?

13:22.780 --> 13:24.820
No way.

13:46.470 --> 13:47.380
Those two...

13:49.880 --> 13:51.960
But isn't that good?

13:52.520 --> 13:54.170
Youth, huh?

13:58.090 --> 13:59.540
Good morning!

14:00.090 --> 14:00.860
Morning.

14:02.400 --> 14:04.070
Are these from Enoshima?

14:04.070 --> 14:04.980
Yeah.

14:05.500 --> 14:06.630
Looks delicious.

14:10.100 --> 14:11.510
Today is hot again.

14:22.710 --> 14:23.810
Good morning!

14:24.120 --> 14:25.550
Oh, you're alone?

14:25.550 --> 14:26.630
Huh?

14:26.630 --> 14:28.800
I heard it from Yamabuki Hiyori.

14:28.800 --> 14:30.610
That the two of you went to the sea, right?

14:32.420 --> 14:34.890
We all wanted to go to the sea too.

14:34.890 --> 14:35.850
Idiot!

14:35.850 --> 14:37.310
Why am I an idiot?

14:37.310 --> 14:38.090
You're dense!

14:38.850 --> 14:41.860
Why do you always speak down to others?

14:42.390 --> 14:45.800
What I meant was that we should leave Suzuki and Gouta alone.

14:46.620 --> 14:47.440
Oh, I see.

14:48.040 --> 14:50.090
Why are you blushing, Kuroda Kouji?

14:54.410 --> 14:55.280
Idiot!

15:04.800 --> 15:05.920
Good morning!

15:05.920 --> 15:06.960
Yo.

15:06.960 --> 15:08.340
Today is really hot.

15:08.340 --> 15:09.200
Yeah.

15:10.360 --> 15:11.970
How was the sea?

15:11.970 --> 15:14.040
Well, the same as usual.

15:14.550 --> 15:16.390
Did Sora-chan have fun?

15:16.390 --> 15:17.190
Um...

15:17.720 --> 15:18.430
Probably.

15:19.310 --> 15:20.840
I wanted to go to the sea too...

15:23.590 --> 15:25.280
Did you invite her?

15:26.100 --> 15:28.980
Midorikawa-kun, I'm moved!

15:28.980 --> 15:30.860
W-Why?

15:30.860 --> 15:32.070
Well...

15:32.070 --> 15:34.990
You didn't know any magic and then suddenly to release so much power...

15:34.990 --> 15:37.530
I'm moved!

15:37.530 --> 15:38.770
Did you see it?

15:39.520 --> 15:42.460
Abe and Mizoguchi were moved too.

15:42.460 --> 15:45.000
I was really moved, Midorikawa-kun.

15:45.000 --> 15:45.920
Me too!

15:45.920 --> 15:47.420
Midorikawa-kun is the best!

15:47.420 --> 15:48.670
I've fallen for you too.

15:48.670 --> 15:50.710
Midorikawa, shake my hand.

15:50.710 --> 15:51.920
Me too.

15:51.920 --> 15:53.630
Please shake our hands!

15:53.630 --> 15:54.370
Ah...

15:58.160 --> 15:58.900
thanks.

16:01.900 --> 16:04.440
So then, tomorrow's lecture will start at 9am.

16:04.440 --> 16:06.690
Please be mindful of the heat, everyone.

16:06.690 --> 16:08.330
Yes.

16:10.300 --> 16:11.510
You seem popular.

16:12.810 --> 16:14.700
Ah, they're just making fun of me.

16:15.170 --> 16:17.960
With that, you're now an impressive mage.

16:18.510 --> 16:21.150
Now you're all stuck up, just like Asagi.

16:27.730 --> 16:30.340
You know, Asagi is written as the kanji for "shallow" and "onion."

16:30.340 --> 16:32.060
Hey, you like her?

16:53.120 --> 16:54.050
All right.

17:08.340 --> 17:09.250
I see.

17:09.250 --> 17:10.080
That's a relief.

17:11.630 --> 17:12.510
I'm soaked.

17:17.930 --> 17:19.360
That was a close one.

17:51.900 --> 17:54.910
Now that the weather has cleared up, let's sing a song.

17:57.990 --> 18:00.340
It's a cover of the Moonriders song.

20:13.710 --> 20:15.880
Pistol Pinoko...

20:17.070 --> 20:18.170
What a weird name.

20:22.750 --> 20:25.250
Hello, the light is on, but...

20:25.920 --> 20:28.280
Ah, we're open.

20:28.280 --> 20:29.290
Then get me a drink,

20:30.200 --> 20:31.160
I want something strong.

20:31.740 --> 20:32.550
Okay.

20:36.930 --> 20:37.800
Did something happen?

20:38.740 --> 20:39.490
Nothing.

20:40.470 --> 20:41.280
High school student?

20:41.660 --> 20:42.520
Social worker.

20:44.720 --> 20:47.300
Still, you look messy.

20:47.300 --> 20:49.000
If you're worrying about money, I can pay.

20:56.770 --> 20:57.810
What's this?

20:57.810 --> 20:58.960
Oolong tea.

21:00.150 --> 21:00.900
If it's money...

21:00.900 --> 21:04.770
Unfortunately, we don't serve alcohol to brats, so don't start complaining.

21:05.420 --> 21:06.360
Damn it.

21:14.190 --> 21:15.800
Stop playing depressing music.

21:21.220 --> 21:23.560
Today, I have no place to go home to.

21:24.210 --> 21:25.470
Would you like some curry?

23:06.380 --> 23:12.000
Although I hate lying, there are times when I can't say the truth...

23:12.850 --> 23:14.470
Next episode: Life

23:15.430 --> 23:18.580
Gouta-kun, I really can't say it after all.

23:18.580 --> 23:19.870
I'm sorry.
